1892–93 was the fifth season of Scottish football for [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]], who competed in the [[Scottish Football League]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1890/celtic1893.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1892-93|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref>

Celtic won the league for the first time by just one point. It was the club's second major domestic honour, as they had won the Scottish Cup the previous season. They failed to retain that trophy, though, as they lost the final replay 2-1 against [[Queen's Park F.C.|Queen's Park]]. Celtic won the originally scheduled final 1-0, but although the match was voided upon pre-match inspection, it was played nonetheless so as to not upset the 30,000 crowd gathered at Ibrox Park, with the decision announced to spectators in the second half.


